      "writtenOn": "2018-06-12T21:08:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes.\n\nWe wont really be leveraging this too much, but I exposed it because I didn\u0027t want a massive refactor in some special one-off cases.\n\nBlueprint prefix is primarily where we will be working, but the structure is designed so you can do:\n\nBlueprint owns /users\nAPI owns /users/API\nand Endpoint can own /users/API/credentials\n\nI expect we will not use this, but exposing it allows for some of the potential future things such as splitting auth and catalog to /auth /catalog instead of version-specific lead but maintaining v3/auth leaning on the same code. There will always be some restructuring to implement, but this limits it.\n\nThis also lets me lean on the bp-prefix for the /v3 addition for now behind the scenes without needing to encode it in the dispatch route definition(s)",
